# ngspice reads the noise summary interval; HSPICE noise is against ground (b855300c, part b).
# What the fix was for, as the ledger has it: the statement reads as `noise` with `interval` = 5
# (not opaque); output has `.noise v(out) vin 5` after an `.ac dec 10 1 1meg` line.
from: ngspice
to: hspice
--- input
t
vin in 0 ac 1
r1 in out 1k
.noise v(out) vin dec 10 1 1meg 5
.end
--- output
t
.option tnom=27
vin in 0 ac 1
r1 in out 1k
.ac dec 10 1 1meg
.noise v(out) vin 5
.end
--- report
warning[caveat]: options: ngspice assumes other defaults for tnom than hspice does; they are written out
warning[caveat]: line 4: noise.src: HSPICE runs noise as part of an AC analysis, so the AC analysis itself is run as well
